  "name": "ad-choke-points",
  "description": "Example 3 (AD choke points). 20 users can reach Domain Admins. The 14 in IT-Helpdesk get there through Workstation-Admins (nested), local admin on ACME-WS-0193 and da-jlee's credentials left there; the 6 in Server-Admins through ACME-JUMP-01, where da-jlee also left credentials, and through ACME-SYNC-01, which stores the MSOL_ directory sync account's credentials, and MSOL_ can replicate Domain Admins. So removing da-jlee's membership cuts off 14 of 20 (70%); the 6 keep the MSOL_ bypass. jlee owns da-jlee: ownership is context, not a way in. Reduced: the example's 1,811 workstations with no admin logons are 5 here (ACME-WS-0001 to 0005), and its aggregated members are listed by name.",
